Problem definition:

Compressible RANS equations.
Turbulence model: Menter's SST
Transition model: Langtry and Menter's transition (2009)
Mach number: 0.1.
Angle of attack (AoA): 4 deg, and angle of sideslip (AoS): 0 deg.
Reynolds number: 300000.
Non-Dimensional simulation (V=Mach, Rho=1.0, T=1.0 at the farfield).
The reference area is 3 m^2.
The reference length is 1 m.


Problem definition:

Viscous flow: Computing pressure using the ideal gas law
based on the free-stream temperature and a density computed
from the Reynolds number.
Force coefficients computed using free-stream values.
-- Input conditions:
Fluid Model: STANDARD_AIR 
Specific gas constant: 287.058 N.m/kg.K.
Specific gas constant (non-dim): 0.714286
Specific Heat Ratio: 1.4000 
Viscosity Model: SUTHERLAND 
Ref. Laminar Viscosity: 1.716e-05 N.s/m^2.
Ref. Temperature: 273.15 K.
Sutherland Constant: 110.4 K.
Laminar Viscosity (non-dim): 3.19679e-07
Ref. Temperature (non-dim): 0.947944
Sutherland constant (non-dim): 0.383134
Conductivity Model: CONSTANT_PRANDTL 
Prandtl: 0.72
Turbulent Conductivity Model: CONSTANT_PRANDTL 
Turbulent Prandtl: 0.9
Free-stream static pressure: 13047.7 Pa.
